Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:58:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: retain previous height in header difficulty
 diagnostics

Convert the upstream bad-diffbits diagnostic to a typed signed previous
height while retaining its readable text, Info severity and rejection path.
This belongs in the shared eCash tier: the original call predates the ABC
base (3e9c4007111), unlike the separate native V2 header metadata checks.

Add a focused public ProcessNewBlockHeaders negative case using bounded
real regtest proof of work. It checks the rejection, unchanged active tip,
readable message and JSON height type. This source-only batch has not been
compiled or run; the immutable validated 381-site delivery is unchanged.

Scripted production diff:
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/header-difficulty-diagnostic.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/difficulty395-conversion.json --apply
